<h1>Charter</h1>

<p>Avatars of Shadows is a diverse guild of friends. We hold friendship, honesty, loyalty, respect amongst us, and the 
populace of Norrath above all else. We have been brought together by the mutual desire to enjoy our time in this diverse 
and mature guild. It is our beliefs that in helping each other achieve their goals and desires, our own will be fulfilled 
more then we could ever hope for.</p>

<p>To promote the ideals of the guild, there will be a guild leader and a council made up of officers, chosen based on 
leadership and reputation. No unruly members will be tolerated! The respect and name of the guild must be placed above all 
issues, actions, or other situations. We want the ability to stand on our own; over time this will be achieved with confidence 
and conviction and with it our respect as a guild will come.</p>

<h1>Rules: </h1>

<p>As all where chosen basted on reputation and conduct in the lands of Norrath, the rules of this family are simple.</p>
<ol>
<li>To have fun, this is very important.  If you are not having fun, there are officers, captains, and a guild leader you can speak to about what is troubling you.  The door is always open, and if you seek something different we will extend our gratitude to you, and wish you well.
<li>Guild helps Guild. The guild comes first whether you are twinking a main or camping; we do things as a family. If you need assistance with something, just ask, many times there are not more pressing matters to attend to.
<li>Kill Stealing, Ninja Looting, and things of this sort are not allowed.  This is shameful to the guild.
<li>Foul language, inappropriate jokes, sexual harassment, and the like will not be tolerated.  This applies to guild chat, shouts, ouch, tells and says.  Spamming will not be tolerated.
<li>Role-play mode is acceptable, but anonymous is not, unless approved by a guild leader or officer.  Don't be ashamed of your guild tag, but do not bring shame to your tag.  We understand that you will not always be in a nice mood, and you are not expected to always be nice and considerate to everyone you meet, but you WILL be respectful to all.  If you are role-playing, and things get out of hand, consider your actions before continuing.
<li>Check the guild boards as often as possible.  This is the way we can all keep contact with each other.
<li>During guild raids, group leaders are too obeyed under all circumstances.  If told to back off of a mob, you will do so immediately.
<li>All guild decisions will be brought to guild leader or officers and guild will vote on rules.  Each officer, class captain and member will receive one vote.
<li>If someone approaches you concerning a problem with a fellow guild member, you are to immediately tell (in this order) the Guild Leader, the Guild Captains (Tadayna or Kilinie), or a Guild Officer.  If not officers are present, you are to give the "complainant(s)" the Guild Leader's email or one of the captain's email, or the public board address, and explain they need to post a way for us to contact them, in game or out of game.
<li>Duels are acceptable (between members or non-members) but looting another guild member's body is not permitted (non-members are fair game).
</ol>

<h1>Position Descriptions:</h1>
<p><u>Guild Leader</u><br>
Has final say in all matters in regards to the guild.</p>
<p><u>Guild Captain</u><br>
Second in command to Guild Leader, has final say if GL is not available.</p>
<p><u>Officers (and class captains)</u><br>
Help in the overall running of the guild.</p>

<h1>Addenda:</h1>
<p>No Dual Guild Tags allowed.</p>

<h1>Joining the family:</h1>
<ol>
<li>Complete the Guild Application and return it via email to Tyrellan (the Guild Leader)
<li>Meet with several members, spend time with them, and see how we work together as a family.
<li>Final decision will be made by vote.
</ol>
<p>Understand that this process can take a few days.  Do not get discouraged.</p>

<h1>Prospective member must do the following:</h1>
<ol>
<li>Seek out members of Avatars of Shadow to hunt with of their own free will, this will show their interest.
<li>Prospective member must have two sponsors within the guild.
<li>These sponsors are required to start a thread in members' only section speaking about you, and what they are learning about you.
<li>Sponsors are responsible for getting to now the prospect, answer their questions and judge the character of prospect.
</ol>

<h1>Members must:</h1>
<ol>
<li>Welcome said prospect into their ranks to hunt. This should be a given, and the member will post their opinion on said person under the appropriate thread in members section. The Guild will use this to determine the prospects worth to the guild and make a final decision on entrance.
</ol>
<p>Upon admittance prospect is tagged and given a 30 day probationary period. Sponsors of said prospect will be contacted if there are any issues with said prospect.</p>

<h1>Guild Bank:</h1>
<p>Tyrellan, Kilinie and Tadayna have the alts which house the Guild Bank.  The rules for the Guild Bank are simple:</p>
<ol>
<li>If you need something for your MAIN character send one of us a tell in game and let us know.  
<li>If you receive something from the guild bank, do your best to replace the item or return it when you are finished with it.
<li>Donations are ALWAYS accepted to the guild bank.
</ol>
<p>There are not enough items to furnish alts with items, so please try to twink your own alts.</p>


<h1>Reprimands:</h1>
<p>1st problem - warning<br>
2nd problem - loss of guild status<br>
3rd problem - immediate de-guilding</p>
